X:6
T:Silly Old Man
% NFF Book 2020
C:Trad
S:J Walsh (pub 1750)
S:see also The Convict Dance Music Research Project, by Dr. Heather Blasdale-Clarke at QUT
Z:transcribed & arranged by Roland Clarke, 2019
N: Other Versions:
N: - VMP - J.Johnson Choice Collection Vol 1, No 96, (c.1750), as "Silly Old man"
N: - John Chambers Online Music Books", O'Farrell Pocket Companion for the Irish or Union Pipes", (1805-1810), No 306, as "Shan Dinna or Silly Old Man, and No 307, as "Shandinna"
N:- Francis O'Neill, "Dance Music of Ireland" No 404, (1907), as "I'm a silly old man"
H:The crew of the "HMS Bounty" are reported to have sung this as they threw 
H:Captain Bligh off his ship.
B:J Walsh, "Caledonian Country Dances, Being a collection of all the celebrated Scotch country dances now in vogue", London N.D.
O:Australia, NSW, Sydney
